.TH STUD 1 "November 2026" "Stud @STUD_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
stud \- play Roblox on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B stud
.RI [ URI ]
.br
.B stud
.RB [ \-\-roblox | \-\-studio ]
.br
.B stud
.RB [ \-\-instance
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-roblox | \-\-studio ]
.br
.B stud \-\-settings
.br
.B stud \-\-install\-desktop\-entry
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Stud
runs the real, unmodified Roblox macOS client on a Linux desktop, in its own
window, with the mouse and keyboard, through Rosemary. There is no emulator
and no virtual machine: Rosemary runs the client's own x86_64 code and
supplies the macOS interfaces it expects around it.
.PP
Roblox is not included. Stud downloads the client from Roblox's own servers
and keeps it up to date before each launch, and Roblox remains subject to its
own terms.
.PP
Run with no arguments, Stud asks whether to open Roblox or Roblox Studio.
Given a
.BR roblox: ,
.B roblox\-player:
or
.B roblox\-studio:
URI \- what a browser hands over when you press Play or Edit on the website \-
it opens straight into that experience.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-roblox
Open Roblox without asking.
.TP
.B \-\-studio
Open Roblox Studio without asking.
.TP
.BI \-\-instance " name"
Run as the instance
.IR name :
its own settings, its own download and update history, and above all its own
macOS environment and Roblox login, kept under
.IR ~/.local/share/stud/instances/name/ ,
so another instance can be signed in to another account at the same time. The
first instance, without a name, keeps the plain paths. The Roblox client itself
is shared, so only the first one to need a build downloads it.
.TP
.B \-\-settings
Open the Settings window on its own, without launching the client. This is
what the desktop entry's Settings action runs.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-desktop\-entry
Register Stud as the handler for Roblox's URIs for the current user, so a
browser can hand a game over to it. A package installs the desktop entry
system-wide already; this exists for an AppImage or a build tree.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/stud/config.json
Settings. Written by the Settings window, and safe to edit by hand.
.TP
.I ~/.config/stud/flags.json
FastFlag overrides, written into the client's own settings at launch.
.TP
.I ~/.config/stud/customizations/
Files laid over Roblox's own content (\fIstudio\-customizations/\fR for
Studio).
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/stud/client/
The macOS client, as Roblox's servers ship it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/stud/prefix/
Rosemary's prefix: Roblox's own settings, login and data.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/stud/logs/
One log per session, Stud's and the client's.
.PP
A named instance, `--instance name`, keeps all of the above under
.IR ~/.config/stud/instances/name/ ,
.IR ~/.local/share/stud/instances/name/ ,
etc., and its session logs under
.IR ~/.local/state/stud/instances/name/logs/ .
Its own Roblox settings and login are in that instance's
.IR prefix/ ,
so each instance is a separate Roblox account.
.SH BUGS
Report at
.UR https://github.com/CatPieLeaf/Stud/issues
.UE .
